.TH TUI_LINEEDIT_INIT 3 2026-10-03 "libtuikit 0.1" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_lineedit_init, tui_lineedit_free, tui_lineedit_set_text,
tui_lineedit_insert, tui_lineedit_handle, tui_lineedit_render,
tui_lineedit_cursor_col, tui_lineedit_run, tui_history_init,
tui_history_free, tui_history_add, tui_history_count, tui_history_get \-
single-line text editor and line history
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/lineedit.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_lineedit_init(tui_lineedit *" le ", char *" buf ", size_t " size ", const char *" initial );
.BI "void tui_lineedit_free(tui_lineedit *" le );
.BI "void tui_lineedit_set_text(tui_lineedit *" le ", const char *" text );
.BI "int  tui_lineedit_insert(tui_lineedit *" le ", const char *" utf8 );
.BI "tui_edit_result tui_lineedit_handle(tui_lineedit *" le ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "int  tui_lineedit_render(tui_lineedit *" le ", tui_canvas " c ", const char *" prompt ", tui_style " st );
.BI "int  tui_lineedit_cursor_col(const tui_lineedit *" le );
.BI "int  tui_lineedit_run(tui_lineedit *" le ", int " in_fd ", int " out_fd ", int " row ", int " col ,
.BI "                      const char *" prompt );
.PP
.BI "void tui_history_init(tui_history *" h ", int " max );
.BI "void tui_history_free(tui_history *" h );
.BI "int  tui_history_add(tui_history *" h ", const char *" line );
.BI "int  tui_history_count(const tui_history *" h );
.BI "const char *tui_history_get(const tui_history *" h ", int " i );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR tui_lineedit
edits one line of UTF-8 text in a buffer the caller owns.
It is a pure model: an event in, the line changed.
The cursor moves and deletes by character \(em a multi-byte character and
the combining marks that belong to it are one \(em and columns are display
columns, so accented and wide text behaves.
.PP
.BR tui_lineedit_init ()
starts editing in
.I buf
(capacity
.IR size ,
NUL included) with
.I initial
text (may be NULL) and the cursor at its end, as email-cli's
.BR input_line_init ().
The members
.IR tab_fn ,
.IR shift_tab_fn ,
.I render_below
(email-cli's completion hooks),
.I history
and
.I user
may be set afterwards.
.BR tui_lineedit_free ()
frees the editor's own memory (the kill buffer, a saved draft), not the
buffer.
.PP
.BR tui_lineedit_insert ()
inserts text at the cursor: a tab, CR or LF becomes a space, other control
characters are dropped, and what does not fit is not inserted \(em never
half a character.
.BR tui_lineedit_set_text ()
replaces the text; completion hooks use it.
.SS Keys
.BR tui_lineedit_handle ()
applies one event and returns what it did:
.B TUI_EDIT_CHANGED
(the event was used),
.B TUI_EDIT_ACCEPT
(Enter),
.B TUI_EDIT_CANCEL
(Esc, Ctrl-C),
.B TUI_EDIT_EOF
(Ctrl-D on an empty line), or
.B TUI_EDIT_IGNORED
(not an editing event \(em the program may use it).
.TS
l l.
characters, paste	insert
Left, Right, Ctrl-B, Ctrl-F	one character
Ctrl+Left, Ctrl+Right, Alt-B, Alt-F	one word
Home, End, Ctrl-A, Ctrl-E	start, end
Backspace, Ctrl-H	delete before the cursor
Delete, Ctrl-D	delete at the cursor
Ctrl-K, Ctrl-U	kill to the end, to the start
Ctrl-W, Alt-Backspace	kill the word before
Ctrl-Y	yank the last kill
Up, Down	older, newer history line
Tab, Shift-Tab	tab_fn, shift_tab_fn
.TE
.PP
Browsing the history keeps the line being edited and brings it back after
the newest entry; Up and Down are ignored without a history, and Tab and
Shift-Tab without their hooks.
.SS Drawing
.BR tui_lineedit_render ()
draws
.I prompt
and the text on the first row of a canvas, scrolled horizontally so the
cursor is visible, places the terminal cursor there and returns its
column.
.PP
.BR tui_lineedit_run ()
is email-cli's
.BR input_line_run ():
a blocking loop that edits on terminal row
.I row
(1-based), reading keys from
.I in_fd
(already in raw mode) and drawing directly to
.I out_fd
\(em no screen needed.
Each draw clears the row, writes
.I prompt
from column
.I col
(1-based; email-cli used 3) followed by the text, calls
.IR render_below ,
then puts the cursor back on the row and shows it.
On return the row below is cleared and the cursor hidden.
It returns 1 on Enter, 0 on Esc or Ctrl-C, and \-1 when the input ended
or failed (which email-cli could not report).
Unlike the original it scrolls a line longer than the terminal.
.SS History
.BR tui_history_init ()
makes an empty history of at most
.I max
lines (256 when
.I max
is 0 or less).
.BR tui_history_add ()
adds a copy of a line, except an empty line or one equal to the most
recent; when full, the oldest line is dropped.
.BR tui_history_get ()
returns line
.IR i ,
0 being the oldest.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_readline (3),
.BR tui_dialog_prompt (3),
